{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the sense of the ephod:</b> for it is larger than the choshen and will not slip off the chest-piece. There are difficult questions concerning the ephod and the choshen. For Moses made only one ephod, yet it is written אפוד ירד בידו (1 Samuel 23:6), and this is not the ephod of Moses, for it does not say the known ephod, as in הגישה האפוד (1 Samuel 23:9). And furthermore, why is ירד written, and not הוריד? For it appears that it was incidental. And there it is written שמנים איש נושא אפוד בד (1 Samuel 22:18), and many interpreters explained this to mean that they were fit to bear an ephod, and they did not pay attention to know the truth, for the ephod of linen (בד) is a type of linen, and the ephod of Moses was not linen but gold, techelet, argaman, and tola'at shani, and shesh with all of them. And they would inquire only by the choshen of judgment, on which were the Urim and Tumim, and thus it is written in the law of the Urim לפני ד' (Numbers 27:21). And there is no objection from הגישה האפוד (1 Samuel 23:9), for the choshen was attached to it, and the Urim with the choshen, and thus it is written עד עמוד הכהן לאורים ותומים (Nehemiah 7:65), and it is written תמיך ואוריך (Deuteronomy 33:8). Now we have seen that HaShem answered David by means of the ephod of Abiathar. And Saul, when he went to war, inquired by the Urim — these are the very ones that were in the choshen of judgment with the ephod and the ark. Yet David inquired at Ziklag by the ephod of Abiathar, and it is not the ephod of Moses. This is a hard question, for the Urim are not the stones of the choshen, for it is written ומלאת בו מלואת אבן (below, verse 17), and this is the work of the craftsman, not the work of Moses. And afterward it is said to Moses, ונתת אל חשן המשפט את האורים ואת התומים (below, verse 30). And in the making of the ephod it is written ארבעה טורי אבן (below, 39:10), and the rows are mentioned, and it is said of Moses, ויתן עליו את החשן, ויתן אל החשן את האורים ואת התומים (Leviticus 8:8). Now according to the plain sense, the stones are not the shining ones or the perfecting ones, for the inquiry is by the Urim and Tumim, and we do not know what they are. And the letters of the names of the tribes are of no avail, nor the names of the patriarchs, for it is not called choshen of judgment except on account of the Urim that are upon it. And there is yet another question: we cannot say that the Urim are themselves the Tumim, for it is written לאורים ותומים (Ezra 2:63), and furthermore the word לאורים and also תומים are plural, and they are many things. And R. Shlomo said that the Urim and Tumim were writings of the explicit Name. And had our master the Gaon [Saadia] seen the answer of R. Shlomo, he would not have said thus. And the matter of the ephod and the choshen is a deep sod. I shall only hint at part of the sod — perhaps he who has knowledge of the knowledge of the Most High will understand it. And the key by which one may enter the sod: the two braided cords placed on the two settings, and the scheme of the ephod is the plane at its midpoint; therefore the six are on the second shoulder, and these are according to thought, therefore they are on one stone, by the number of the children of Israel and by their names according to their generations, and likewise the second six — only the law is not according to the inward division but according to the division as seen by the eye. And on account of the inclination it says וירכסו את החשן מטבעותיו אל טבעות האפוד בפתיל תכלת (Exodus 28:28). And the choshen was double, for there the Urim and Tumim were kept until the time of need; then they would place them outside the choshen. Now the shoham stones are equal, of one kind, and the stones of the choshen are not so, for the shoham are for a remembrance, and the judgment of the children of Israel is upon the stones of the choshen. And the word אורים is from the root of חמותי ראיתי אור (Isaiah 44:13), and תומים — they are תמימים. And the Urim, not the Tumim, were gold and silver, and their number is known by complete proofs from above and below, and the discerning will understand. Now there were many ephods with the priests, and they have a scheme, only there is no choshen and no Urim. And one who was practiced in the matters of the Urim and Tumim that were upon the choshen of judgment could answer the inquirer by means of the likeness of the ephod alone — but not at every time. And had I undertaken to reveal this sod, I could not have written it according to the format of the commentary I composed on the entire book, for none would understand it who has not studied Sefer Ha-Midot and Sod Ma'aseh Shamayim. And there is no need to elaborate on the form of the ephod and the choshen and the rings."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Resolved רבינו האי as 'our master the Gaon [Saadia]' based on the voice rules; the referent of רבינו שלמה is Rashi (R. Shlomo Yitzhaki). The citation ישעי' מ\"ד likely points to Isaiah 44, but the quoted phrase חמותי ראיתי אור does not correspond to any verse at that location and may reflect a textual corruption or a paraphrastic reference."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:10.101981219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}